1
00:00:00,632 --> 00:00:03,110
Now let's assume that submitting a goal

2
00:00:03,224 --> 00:00:04,260
takes a bit longer.

3
00:00:05,184 --> 00:00:07,209
And we can actually simulate this by going

4
00:00:07,209 --> 00:00:09,282
to this postGoals handler here.

5
00:00:10,105 --> 00:00:13,025
And then there we can use the setTimeout

6
00:00:13,025 --> 00:00:13,477
function

7
00:00:14,074 --> 00:00:16,123
to set a timeout of 1 second, let's say.

8
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:20,290
And then I only send the response after that

9
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:21,227
timeout expired.

10
00:00:22,245 --> 00:00:24,072
So now it will take 1 second for the

11
00:00:24,072 --> 00:00:26,448
response to arrive. And with that, I'm just

12
00:00:26,512 --> 00:00:28,209
simulating a slower backend.

13
00:00:29,017 --> 00:00:30,236
If we do that,

14
00:00:30,798 --> 00:00:32,594
you will see that if we reload here

15
00:00:33,188 --> 00:00:35,129
and we send a new request,

16
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:36,925
it'll still work like before.

17
00:00:37,535 --> 00:00:38,834
But now you can of course see

18
00:00:39,364 --> 00:00:41,770
that the input is only reset after the

19
00:00:41,770 --> 00:00:42,556
response arrived.

20
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:45,620
And therefore there is this time window

21
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:48,122
where we could hammer this button because we

22
00:00:48,122 --> 00:00:49,341
don't understand

23
00:00:49,871 --> 00:00:50,223
that

24
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:53,785
a request was on its way because the input

25
00:00:53,817 --> 00:00:55,068
wasn't cleared immediately.

26
00:00:55,806 --> 00:00:58,177
And we therefore by accident might send an

27
00:00:58,305 --> 00:01:00,565
extra request which we don't wanna send.

28
00:01:01,574 --> 00:01:03,818
Now, of course, one solution for this

29
00:01:03,818 --> 00:01:04,170
problem

30
00:01:04,795 --> 00:01:07,295
would be to immediately clear the input

31
00:01:07,295 --> 00:01:09,682
again right after a goal was submitted.

32
00:01:10,419 --> 00:01:12,471
So back on this form here, instead of

33
00:01:12,471 --> 00:01:15,002
listening to after request, we could again

34
00:01:15,115 --> 00:01:17,021
listen to the built-in submit event again.

35
00:01:17,935 --> 00:01:20,483
But maybe we only wanna clear it after we

36
00:01:20,483 --> 00:01:22,149
know that the request succeeded.

37
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:26,143
In that case, a better workaround would be

38
00:01:26,143 --> 00:01:29,363
to simply disable this button whilst the

39
00:01:29,379 --> 00:01:30,755
request is on its way.

40
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:34,017
And since this is such a common requirement,

41
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:36,023
HTMX has got us covered.

42
00:01:36,719 --> 00:01:41,513
It offers an hx-disabled-elt

43
00:01:42,388 --> 00:01:42,972
attribute,

44
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,564
and elt stands for element.

45
00:01:46,662 --> 00:01:48,836
And what this attribute does is

46
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:50,193
it allows you

47
00:01:50,776 --> 00:01:53,137
to specify a CSS selector

48
00:01:53,748 --> 00:01:56,269
of an element you wanna disable here as a

49
00:01:56,269 --> 00:01:57,939
value for this attribute.

50
00:01:58,967 --> 00:02:01,922
And it'll then go ahead and add the disabled

51
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:04,990
attribute and set this element to disabled,

52
00:02:05,568 --> 00:02:07,993
this element you're targeting here, whenever

53
00:02:07,993 --> 00:02:10,772
some request for this element on which you

54
00:02:10,852 --> 00:02:12,715
added this attribute is on its way.

55
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:16,264
So whenever this POST request is on its way,

56
00:02:16,329 --> 00:02:16,987
for example.

57
00:02:18,336 --> 00:02:21,035
So here I can target this button

58
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:25,195
by using button as a CSS selector or

59
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:26,721
form-button

60
00:02:27,251 --> 00:02:29,500
to look for a button inside of a form, which

61
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:31,363
is definitely only this button.

62
00:02:32,552 --> 00:02:35,170
And then this button will be disabled due to

63
00:02:35,202 --> 00:02:38,383
this attribute whenever this POST request is

64
00:02:38,559 --> 00:02:39,089
on its way.

65
00:02:40,519 --> 00:02:42,511
So with that, if we reload,

66
00:02:43,234 --> 00:02:45,902
and I again learn HTMX, you see that now the

67
00:02:45,966 --> 00:02:47,026
button is disabled

68
00:02:47,718 --> 00:02:49,646
and it's disabled for the duration of the

69
00:02:49,646 --> 00:02:52,379
request after which it is enabled again. But

70
00:02:52,379 --> 00:02:54,344
of course then the input was cleared

71
00:02:54,875 --> 00:02:57,097
due to this event handler code here.

72
00:02:58,857 --> 00:03:01,035
And therefore this is another very useful

73
00:03:01,133 --> 00:03:03,213
attribute and feature you should be aware

74
00:03:03,343 --> 00:03:03,392
of.
